## small-bodies

small-bodies-ask = How to measure a millet grain better than to a millimetre?
small-bodies-title = Measuring small bodies by the method of rows
small-bodies-question = The ruler’s divisions are 1 mm, and a millet grain is only about two divisions across, a pea six or seven. We measure one pea, then a row of peas, a row of millet, and wind a thread on a rod. How to measure a grain better than to a millimetre?
small-bodies-choices = Lay many grains in a row and divide the row’s length by their number
small-bodies-choices-2 = Measure one grain very carefully
small-bodies-choices-3 = No way: a ruler measures no better than its division
small-bodies-setup = A ruler with millimetre divisions, peas, millet, two toothpicks, a pen refill, a № 10 thread (≈ 50 cm)
